    "created_at": "2016-06-09T15:20:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-09T15:20:29Z",
    "body": "> We need to have a response variable set to null early on (before \"Fragments:\") that can be updated by various concepts along the way.\n\nWhile this is true, we also use _resource_ for this. So if we also started using a _response_ this would become somewhat confusing.\n\nWe might just have to extract the bit starting at \"Fragments\" into its own algorithm somehow so that directs (anything else?) can invoke that with different arguments later on...\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
